<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU Presidency calls for extra 500mln Ecus beef aid.</title>
<headline>EU Presidency calls for extra 500mln Ecus beef aid.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Irish EU Presidency proposed on Wednesday, the third day of a farm ministers' meeting, an extra 500 milllion Ecus aid to help beef producers affected by the mad cow crisis.</p>
<p>&quot;The (Farm) Council considers that the continuing serious difficulties justify additional measures (including promotion) for the beef sector amounting to not less than 500 Mecus,&quot; it said in a new compromise paper.</p>
<p>EU farm ministers rejected an initial Irish compromise proposal on Tuesday, saying aid was insufficient.</p>
<p>French Farm Minister Philippe Vasseur, backed by Germany and other member states, warned on Tuesday that if extra aid was not provided there would be a crisis.</p>
<p>But EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler has said there is no more money available in the farm budget.</p>
<p>No immediate reaction was available on the new text.</p>
</text>
